  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Pair passing – standing and on the move",
  "description": "Players pair up with one ball per pair. Start standing still 5–8 metres apart and pass back and forth. Stop and control the ball before playing it back. Push the pass along the ice with the stick rather than hitting it.\n\nOnce that works, the pairs skate across or along the rink side by side at the same distance and pass as they go. The pass should arrive in front of the partner's stick so they can take it without losing speed. Turn at the board or end line and come back.\n\nVariant: first-time passes only, or switch sides in the pair so both pass in both directions. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stick on the ice with the blade angled towards your partner – show where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Soften the reception: give a little with the stick as the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Push the ball with firm, flat passes – no chopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Eyes up and eye contact before you pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
